# megane / sprout-app rules for Cursor AI

## Read these files first (in order)
1. `AGENTS.md` — checklist and hot paths (start here, most token-efficient)
2. `sprout.index.json` — same as structured JSON (skills table, file paths, pitfalls)
3. `CLAUDE.md` — full architecture detail (read when you need more depth)

## Stack
Go + Gin + SQLite3 (CGO required) · Gemini LLM (structured output via JSON schema) · Plain HTML/JS frontend · JWT auth

## The three surfaces that change in every sprout
1. `prompts/system.txt` — what the LLM does and what fields it populates
2. `internal/models/document_analysis.go` — Go struct whose `json`+`description` tags drive the Gemini JSON schema
3. `static/js/analyze.js` → `renderAnalysis()` (~line 161) — renders the result modal

**These three must stay in sync.** Adding a field to the struct without updating the prompt and renderer is the most common mistake.

## LLM output model rules
- Every output struct must implement `models.LLMOutput` (one method: `SchemaName() string`)
- Use `json:"field"` + `description:"hint for gemini"` on every field. `description` is passed verbatim to Gemini.
- Register structs via `pipe.Routes` in `cmd/server/main.go`
- Default struct: `models.DocumentAnalysis` in `internal/models/document_analysis.go`

## Pipeline route registration (`cmd/server/main.go`)
```go
pipe.Routes = []pipeline.Route{
    {
        Name:      "my-domain",
        Matches:   func(mime string) bool { return mime == "application/pdf" },
        OutputFor: func(_ string) models.LLMOutput { return &models.MyStruct{} },
        // Process: nil → built-in document analysis flow
    },
    // nil Matches = catch-all, place last
}
```

## File converter rules (`internal/fileconv/`)
- One file per format, implements `Converter` interface: `Extract(ctx, path) (string, error)` + `SupportedMIME() []string`
- Register in `init()` in `converter.go`
- Add MIME type to `allowedMIMETypes` in `internal/handlers/files.go`

## Database rules
- Migrations: `internal/db/migrations.sql` — **append only**, `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`
- Query helpers: methods on `*DB` in `internal/db/db.go`
- Follow existing scan/exec pattern in `db.go`

## API endpoint rules
- User-facing endpoints: `internal/handlers/` + register in `/api` group in `router.go` with `auth.AuthRequired()`
- Admin endpoints: `internal/admin/` + register in `/api/admin` group with `auth.AdminRequired()`
- Return `gin.H{"data": ..., "error": nil}` on success; include HTTP status codes (400/404/500)

## CSS / UI rules
- All design tokens are CSS vars in `:root` in `static/css/style.css`
- Brand color: `--accent` · Layout width: `--layout-max-width` · Modal: `--modal-wide-max-width`
- Always use `escHtml()` before inserting LLM or user data into `innerHTML`

## Commands
```
make run    # dev server (sets CGO_ENABLED=1)
make test
cp .env.example .env  # fill GEMINI_API_KEY + SESSION_SECRET; SQLite defaults to ./.db/megane.db
```

## Pitfalls
- Struct ↔ prompt drift: if Gemini returns null/empty for a field, check that the prompt mentions it
- Renderer gap: new struct fields invisible until `renderAnalysis()` is updated
- CGO: SQLite + PDF require `CGO_ENABLED=1` — never use `go run` without it (use `make run`)
- Go module rename: update all `import "megane/..."` paths when changing `go.mod` module name
